# SealedSecret manifests. `spec.encryptedData` values are CIPHERTEXT, encrypted
# against the cluster's published public cert; only the in-cluster controller
# holds the private key. Being safe to commit is the entire point of Sealed
# Secrets — see FuzeInfra docs/SECRETS_MANAGEMENT.md.
#
# generic.secrets.security.detected-generic-secret fires on the base64 blobs
# anyway, and re-fires the moment a diff touches ANY key in the file, so every
# routine credential rotation would turn this check red for a finding that is a
# false positive by construction.
#
# SCOPE NOTE: this directory holds ONLY SealedSecrets. The trade-off is that a
# *plaintext* v1/Secret accidentally committed HERE would no longer be caught by
# this rule — so keep the directory to sealed manifests only. Detection is
# unchanged everywhere else in the repo, which is where a real leak would land.
deploy/contabo/sealed/

