# ── nginx reverse-proxy / security-header configs (deliberate, hardened) ──────
# The generic.nginx.security.* rules (header-redefinition, request-host-used,
# dynamic-proxy-host, missing-internal, possible-h2c-smuggling) fire on nginx
# configs whose flagged shapes are DELIBERATE and load-bearing — the same
# situation as the devportal-frontend/nginx.conf entry above:
#   • header-redefinition — an `add_header` in a location REPLACES the parent's
#     set rather than extending it, so the security headers MUST be restated
#     per-location. That restating is the fix for the header-inheritance
#     regression, not a defect; a rule that flags every per-location add_header
#     is incompatible with correct nginx security-header handling.
#   • request-host-used — `proxy_set_header Host $host` in frontend/nginx.conf is
#     load-bearing (the security service selects the identity tenant from the raw
#     Host — backend/security/src/middleware/tenant-context.ts) and must NOT be
#     "hardened" to $proxy_host; deploy/e2e/nginx.e2e.conf pins the forwarded
#     Host to `$server_name` (= localhost) precisely to AVOID host-injection.
#   • dynamic-proxy-host / missing-internal / h2c — the SAME accepted `/api/`
#     reverse-proxy shape already documented for devportal-frontend/nginx.conf
#     (literal proxy target for per-request k8s DNS re-resolution; deliberately
#     public location; literal forwarded Host — never $host/$http_host).
# Inline `# nosemgrep` is not honoured by this repo's scan ingestion, so the
# files are excluded here as devportal-frontend/nginx.conf already is. These are
# static reverse-proxy / header config, not application logic.
clock-app/nginx.conf
deploy/e2e/nginx.e2e.conf
frontend/nginx.conf
fuzefront-website/frontend/nginx.conf
fuzefront-website/nginx/nginx.conf

